    "title": "Phrygian: The Note Above Home",
    "summary": "Phrygian is A natural minor with the 2 lowered, which puts a note a half step above home — the strongest single darkening move in the set — and its vamp is two chords a semitone apart.",
    "tags": ["modes", "ear", "theory"],
    "readingTimeMin": 4,
    "publishedAt": "2026-08-15"
  },
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "A Phrygian is A natural minor with the "
        },
        {
          "text": "2",
          "marks": ["code"]
        },
        {
          "text": " lowered to a "
        },
        {
          "text": "b2",
          "marks": ["code"]
        },
        {
          "text": " — "
        },
        {
          "text": "B",
          "marks": ["code"]
        },
        {
          "text": " becomes "
        },
        {
          "text": "Bb",
          "marks": ["code"]
        },
        {
          "text": ", and nothing else moves. "
        },
        {
          "text": "A Bb C D E F G",
          "marks": ["code"]
        },
        {
          "text": ", degrees "
        },
        {
          "text": "1 b2 b3 4 5 b6 b7",
          "marks": ["code"]
        },
        {
          "text": ". Spell it "
        },
        {
          "text": "Bb",
          "marks": ["code"]
        },
        {
          "text": ", never "
        },
        {
          "text": "A#",
          "marks": ["code"]
        },
        {
          "text": " — that's what the app's own scale builder prints, and the chip beside this prose says the same. Its parent major is "
        },
        {
          "text": "F",
          "marks": ["code"]
        },
        {
          "text": ", named once and put down."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The characteristic note is the "
        },
        {
          "text": "b2",
          "marks": [
            "code",
            {
              "type": "color",
              "tone": "rose"
            }
