    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Harmonise A natural minor and the chord built on the "
        },
        {
          "text": "2",
          "marks": ["code"]
        },
        {
          "text": " is "
        },
        {
          "text": "Bdim",
          "marks": ["code"]
        },
        {
          "text": " — "
        },
        {
          "text": "The Chords A Minor Gives You",
          "link": {
            "kind": "article",
            "slug": "minor-caged-the-chords-of-the-key"
          }
        },
        {
          "text": " called it the key's least useful chord, with no barre shape at all. Lower the "
        },
        {
          "text": "2",
          "marks": ["code"]
        },
        {
          "text": " to a "
        },
        {
          "text": "b2",
          "marks": ["code"]
        },
        {
          "text": " and a "
        },
        {
          "text": "major",
          "marks": ["bold"]
        },
        {
          "text": " triad, "
        },
        {
          "text": "Bb",
          "marks": ["code"]
        },
        {
          "text": ", stands in exactly that spot instead."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "One more thing worth knowing before you write this off as a curiosity: "
        },
        {
          "text": "Bb",
          "marks": ["code"]
        },
        {
          "text": " major also fits inside one other mode of the seven, and its home chord isn't "
        },
        {
          "text": "Am",
          "marks": ["code"]
        },
        {
          "text": ". So this vamp still does the job of pinning Phrygian down."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The associations are real, and worth naming as exactly that — associations. Phrygian sounds Spanish because flamenco is built on it, not because a "
        },
        {
          "text": "b2",
          "marks": ["code"]
        },
        {
          "text": " is inherently Spanish; "
        },
        {
          "text": "What \"Brighter\" Actually Means",
          "link": {
            "kind": "article",
            "slug": "modes-what-brighter-means"
          }
        },
        {
          "text": " already made that case. Its place in heavy metal is the same kind of claim: the settled reading of the theory literature about what the repertoire does, not something anyone measured. And in the one place this pathway has actual listener data, Phrygian was judged the happier of its pair in just "
        },
        {
          "text": ".21",
          "marks": ["code"]
        },
        {
          "text": " of trials, the lowest of the six tested. The app's own line for it: \"Minor with a ♭2 leaning on the root — Spanish, dark.\""
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Hold an "
        },
